Cesca — a tiny dachshund that lives in your macOS menu bar and nudges you to
journal, check in on what you're doing, and take breaks.

Build:
    ./build-app.sh
    open Cesca.app

Add your own dachshund:
    Drop a transparent PNG at Sources/Cesca/Resources/dachshund.png
    (~40×40 looks best). Rebuild. Until then it falls back to 🐕.

Use:
    Click the dachshund in the menu bar for the last nudge plus controls:
      • Nudge me now
      • Snooze 15/30/60/180 min
      • Interval presets (Pushy / Balanced / Chill / Background)
      • Quit

Nudges go through macOS Notification Center, so accept the permission prompt
on first launch. To auto-start at login: System Settings → General → Login
Items → add Cesca.app.
